// docs/doxygen_mainpage.dox
//
// This file is read by Doxygen only (file pattern `*.dox` is ignored
// by C++ compilation). It adds a landing page and namespace summary
// pages so the public function catalog becomes discoverable from the
// "Namespaces" tab.

/// @mainpage numkit — C++ MATLAB-compatible runtime
///
/// @section nav Quick navigation
///
/// numkit is a C++ runtime with a MATLAB-compatible script engine
/// and a public C++ library API. Most of the **API surface is free
/// functions inside `numkit::<lib>` namespaces** — not classes.
///
/// To browse the function catalog:
///
/// - **Namespaces** tab (top) → pick a sub-namespace below to see every
///   function, struct, and enum exposed by that library:
///   - @ref numkit::builtin "numkit::builtin"  — array / matrix / linalg
///     / strings / types / I/O builtins (the bulk of the surface)
///   - @ref numkit::stats   "numkit::stats"    — descriptive statistics,
///     distributions, hypothesis tests, regression, fit, spline, PCA, …
///   - @ref numkit::signal  "numkit::signal"   — DSP: filter design /
///     analysis / implementation, transforms, windows, measurements
///   - @ref numkit::image   "numkit::image"    — colour, morphology,
///     transforms, quality metrics
///   - @ref numkit::audio   "numkit::audio"    — pitch, harmonics,
///     spectral shape, cepstral, mel
///   - @ref numkit::wavelet "numkit::wavelet"  — DWT / SWT / wavelet
///     filters / wavelet denoising
///   - @ref numkit::control "numkit::control"  — LTI conversions, freq
///     response, time response, props
///   - @ref numkit::comm    "numkit::comm"     — modulation, channels,
///     source coding, equalisation
///
/// - **Files** tab — same content browsable by physical layout
///   (`toolboxes/<lib>/include/numkit/<lib>/.../*.hpp`).
///
/// - **Classes** tab — small set; mostly named-return structs
///   (e.g. @ref numkit::builtin::BalanceResult,
///   @ref numkit::stats::EllipKE).
///
/// @section conv API conventions
///
/// All public functions follow @ref public_api_rules:
/// - Last parameter is always `std::pmr::memory_resource *mr = nullptr`.
/// - Numeric data inputs are `const Value &` (handles any numeric
///   class — DOUBLE / SINGLE / INT* / LOGICAL — via `elemAsDouble`).
/// - Structural inputs (shape vectors, permutations, window
///   descriptors) are `Span<const T>` for type-safe small spans.
/// - Optional `Value`-typed args default to `Value::Empty` and are
///   checked via `isEmpty()`.
///
/// @section build Building the docs
///
/// ```bash
/// cmake --build build/<preset> --target docs       # HTML (this site)
/// cmake --build build/<preset> --target docs-pdf   # PDF reference
/// ```
///
/// LaTeX formulas (`@f$ ... @f$`) render via MathJax in HTML and via
/// pdflatex (MiKTeX / TeX Live) in PDF.
///
/// @section trademark Compatibility &amp; trademark
///
/// numkit is built for compatibility with **MATLAB R2025b**
/// semantics. MATLAB is a registered trademark of The MathWorks, Inc.
/// numkit is an independent project and is **not affiliated with,
/// endorsed by, or sponsored by** The MathWorks, Inc.; references to
/// MATLAB describe interoperability only.

// ── Namespace stubs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Each @namespace block triggers Doxygen to emit a dedicated summary
// page listing every function, struct, and enum inside that namespace.
// The pages are linked from the "Namespaces" tab.

/// @namespace numkit
/// @brief Root namespace for the numkit library.
///
/// Top-level. Most user-facing API lives in the sub-namespaces listed
/// on the @ref index "main page".

/// @namespace numkit::builtin
/// @brief MATLAB-language builtins — the bulk of the public API.
///
/// Covers MATLAB's language-level builtins:
/// - **Math:** `sin`, `cos`, `exp`, `log`, `gamma`, `besselj`, etc.
///   (`numkit/builtin/math/`).
/// - **Arithmetic / reductions:** `sum`, `prod`, `mean`, `max`, `min`,
///   `linspace`, `logspace`, `cumsum`, `diff`, …
/// - **Linear algebra:** `inv`, `lu_decompose`, `qr_decompose`,
///   `svd_decompose`, `chol`, `eig_symmetric`, `expm`, `pinv`, `rank_of`,
///   `norm_value`, `cond_2norm` — see `language/arrays/matrix.hpp`.
/// - **Array manipulation:** `reshape`, `permute`, `cat`, `horzcat`,
///   `vertcat`, `repmat`, `circshift`, `tril`, `triu`, `flip`, …
/// - **Types & casts:** `toDouble`, `int8`..`int64`, `uint8`..`uint64`,
///   `single`, `logical`, `isnumeric`, `isfinite`, `isnan`, `class`, …
/// - **Strings:** `sprintf`, `num2str`, `str2double`, `strcmp`, `regexp`,
///   `split`, `join`, `compose`, …
/// - **Cells / structs:** `cell`, `cellfun`, `cell2mat`, `struct`,
///   `fieldnames`, `isfield`, `rmfield`, `structfun`.
/// - **Interpolation:** `interp1`, `interp2`, `interp3`, `spline`,
///   `pchip`, `mkpp`, `ppval`.
/// - **Polynomials:** `polyfit`, `polyval`, `roots`, `poly`, `polyder`,
///   `polyint`.
/// - **Random:** `rand`, `randn`, `randi`, `randperm`, `rngSeed`, …
/// - **Bitwise / I/O / programming primitives.**

/// @namespace numkit::stats
/// @brief Statistics Toolbox parity.
///
/// - **Descriptive:** `var`, `std`, `median`, `quantile`, `prctile`,
///   `cov`, `corrcoef`, `iqr`, `mad`, `range`, `zscore`, …
/// - **Distributions** (`stats/distributions/`): `normpdf` / `normcdf` /
///   `norminv` / `normrnd` / `normstat` + similar 5-tuple for binomial,
///   poisson, gamma, beta, chi², F, t, weibull, exponential, lognormal,
///   rayleigh, rician, nakagami, GEV, GP, NCX², negbin, hypergeometric,
///   discrete uniform, continuous uniform, extreme value.
/// - **Hypothesis tests:** `ttest`, `ttest2`, `ztest`, `vartest`,
///   `vartest2`, `kstest`, `kstest2`, `jbtest`, `signtest`, `vartestn`,
///   `fishertest`, `chi2gof`, `runstest`, `ranksum`, `signrank`.
/// - **Moving windows:** `movmean`, `movmedian`, `movsum`, `movstd`,
///   `movvar`, `movmin`, `movmax`, `movmad`, `movprod`, `smoothdata`,
///   `hampel`.
/// - **NaN-aware:** `nansum`, `nanmean`, `nanstdev`, `nanvar`,
///   `nanmedian`, `nanmax`, `nanmin`.
/// - **Fitters:** `normfit`, `expfit`, `lognfit`, `binofit`, `raylfit`,
///   `unifit`, `poissfit` + `*like` (negative-log-likelihood) for each.
/// - **Regression / clustering / PCA / spline / QMC / resampling.**

/// @namespace numkit::signal
/// @brief Signal Toolbox: DSP primitives.
///
/// Filter design / analysis / implementation, transforms (FFT, DCT,
/// Hilbert), windows, measurements, multirate, convolution, smoothing,
/// spectral analysis, time-frequency.

/// @namespace numkit::image
/// @brief Image Processing Toolbox.
///
/// Colour-space conversions (`rgb2hsv`, `rgb2lab`, …), 16 standard
/// colormaps (`hot`, `cool`, `jet`, …), morphology (`imerode`,
/// `imdilate`, `imreconstruct`, `bwmorph`, …), transforms
/// (`dct2`, `psf2otf`, `integralImage`, `normxcorr2`, …), type
/// conversions (`im2double`, `im2uint8`, …), quality metrics
/// (`immse`, `psnr`, `ssim`).

/// @namespace numkit::audio
/// @brief Audio Toolbox.
///
/// Pitch & harmonics (`pitch`, `pitchCEP`, `pitchPEF`, `pitchLHS`,
/// `pitchSRH`, `harmonicRatio`), spectral shape (`spectralCentroid`,
/// `spectralSpread`, `spectralRolloffPoint`, `spectralFlux`, …),
/// cepstral (`mfcc`, …), mel-spectrogram, frequency-scale conversions.

/// @namespace numkit::wavelet
/// @brief Wavelet Toolbox.
///
/// 1-D / 2-D DWT, SWT / MODWT, undecimated wavelet transforms,
/// wavelet filters (`wfilters`, `orthfilt`, `qmf`), continuous wavelets
/// (`gauswavf`, `mexihat`, `morlet`, `meyeraux`, …), wavelet
/// reconstruction (`appcoef`, `detcoef`, `waverec`, `wrcoef`),
/// denoising (`wnoisest`).

/// @namespace numkit::control
/// @brief Control System Toolbox.
///
/// LTI conversions (`tf2ss`, `ss2tf`, `tf2zp`, `zp2tf`, `zpk`), frequency
/// response (`bode`, `nyquist`, `freqresp`), time response (`step`,
/// `impulse`, `lsim`), properties (`pole`, `zero`, `dcgain`, `damp`).

/// @namespace numkit::comm
/// @brief Communications Toolbox.
///
/// Modulation (PSK, QAM, APSK, FSK, OFDM, generic-QAM, analog,
/// MIL-188), channel models, source coding (Huffman, arithmetic
/// coding, DPCM, Lloyd quantisation), equalisation, scrambling.

/// @namespace numkit::builtin::detail
/// @brief Implementation detail of @ref numkit::builtin.
///
/// Not part of the stable public API.

/// @namespace numkit::stats::detail
/// @brief Implementation detail of @ref numkit::stats.
///
/// Not part of the stable public API.
